    "derivation": [
      {
        "claim": "Palette_Compose runs in the main loop AFTER the state dispatch, so a compose is followed by the VBlank the next tick's VSync_Wait returns from",
        "from": "engine/system/game_loop.emp, proc GameLoop"
      },
      {
        "claim": "Enqueue_Dirty_Buffers, which queues the palette DMA, runs in VBlank",
        "from": "engine/system/vblank.emp"
      },
      {
        "claim": "Palette_Compose composes base, cycling, cross-fade and operators over lines 1-3, so Pal_Fade_Frames == 0 settles ONE of four",
        "from": "engine/effects/palette.emp, proc Palette_Compose"
      },
      {
        "claim": "the cycling layer's own gate is `btst #1, Pal_Active`, so the `layer` clause tests that bit and NOT Pal_Cycle_Script, which holds the non-zero Pal_Cycle_None sentinel in steady state",
        "from": "engine/effects/palette.emp, Palette_Compose `.cycling`"
      },
      {
        "claim": "the arrival comparison is masked with $0EEE, so `buf` and `cram` compare exactly the bits the engine compares",
        "from": "engine/effects/palette.emp, proc Palette_DoFade `.arrived` test"
      },
      {
        "claim": "a snap install CANCELS a fade in flight with `clr.b Pal_Fade_Frames`, so a 0 count alone cannot tell `arrived` from `stopped`",
        "from": "engine/effects/palette.emp, proc Palette_LoadPal snap arm"
      },
      {
        "claim": "every writer of Palette_Buffer is enumerated by the frame-top palette committer census (14 entries), and every lines-1-3 writer in it is guarded by a flag clauses 1-3 read",
        "from": "engine/system/buffers.emp, pal_committer_census"
      },
      {
        "claim": "N = 1 (compose -> CRAM) + 1 (CRAM -> the completed frame a paused screenshot returns) + 1 (N samples span N-1 intervals) = 3",
        "from": "this module's header"
      }
    ]
